+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional calendar-day `dueDate`; `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only overdue todos; the list page shows the date, marks overdue todos, and has a "nur überfällige" checkbox.
+
+**Architecture:** The overdue rule lives only in `src/store.mjs` (`list({ overdue })`, with an injectable clock `createStore({ now })`). `src/app.mjs` maps the query parameter. `public/index.html` loads `/todos` and `/todos?overdue=true` and marks todos whose id is in the second response.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, builtins only, `node --test`, plain HTML + module script.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-due-date-design.md` (Ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` → HTTP 400.
+- `dueDate` is `"YYYY-MM-DD"` or `null`; every todo in responses carries `dueDate` (default `null`).
+- Overdue = `done === false` and `dueDate` < today in **UTC**; no `dueDate` → never overdue.
+- No `overdue` field on todo responses. No styling (no colour). No create/edit form on the page.
+- New UI elements carry `data-testid`: `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`, `filter-overdue`.
+- UI copy (German, exact): `" · fällig TT.MM.JJJJ"`, `"überfällig"`, `"nur überfällige"`.
+- TDD: failing test in `test/` first.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. Due date == today (UTC) is **not** overdue; yesterday is — boundary test in Task 2.
+2. Impossible/odd dates: `2026-02-30`, `2026-02-29` → 400, `2028-02-29` → OK, `""`, `"2026-1-5"`, `20261023` → 400 — Task 1.
+3. A rejected POST (bad `dueDate`) must not consume an id — Task 1.
+4. `PATCH` without `dueDate` keeps it; `PATCH { dueDate: null }` clears it — Task 1.
+5. Done todo with past date is excluded from the filter; un-done again it reappears — Task 2.
+
+Builder calls (not from the user): only the exact value `overdue=true` filters; any other value (or absence) returns the full list. Dates are formatted by splitting the string, never via `Date` in the browser (avoids timezone shifts).
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: `dueDate` field with validation
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: todos shaped `{ id, title, done, dueDate }`; `store.add({ title, dueDate })`, `store.update(id, patch)` accepting `dueDate`. Internal helper `checkDueDate(value)` throwing `ValidationError('dueDate must be YYYY-MM-DD or null')`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests** (in `test/app.test.mjs`)
+  - Update `creates and lists todos`: expected list becomes `[{ id: 1, title: 'Milch kaufen', done: false, dueDate: null }]`.
+  - `stores a due date`: POST `{ title: 'A', dueDate: '2026-10-24' }` → 201, body `dueDate === '2026-10-24'`.
+  - `rejects invalid due dates`: for each of `'2026-02-30'`, `'2026-02-29'`, `''`, `'2026-1-5'`, `20261023`, `'2026-10-24T00:00:00Z'` POST → 400. Then POST `{ title: 'ok' }` → body `id === 1` (no id consumed).
+  - `accepts a leap day`: POST `dueDate: '2028-02-29'` → 201.
+  - `patches and clears a due date`: POST `{ title: 'A' }`; PATCH `{ dueDate: '2026-11-01' }` → `'2026-11-01'`; PATCH `{ title: 'B' }` → `dueDate` still `'2026-11-01'`; PATCH `{ dueDate: null }` → `null`; PATCH `{ dueDate: 'x' }` → 400.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests, verify they fail** — `npm test`; expected: the new/updated tests FAIL (missing `dueDate`, 201 instead of 400).
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** in `src/store.mjs`: `checkDueDate` accepts `null`/`undefined` (→ `null`) or a string matching `/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/` whose `new Date(value + 'T00:00:00Z').toISOString().slice(0, 10) === value`; otherwise throws. `add` validates title and dueDate **before** `nextId++`. `update` applies `dueDate` only when `'dueDate' in patch`, validating all fields before mutating.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests, verify they pass** — `npm test`; expected: all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** — `git add src/store.mjs test/app.test.mjs && git commit -m "feat: add dueDate to todos (#1)"`
+
+### Task 2: Overdue filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`, `src/app.mjs`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: Task 1 todo shape.
+- Produces: `createStore({ now = () => new Date() } = {})`; `store.list({ overdue = false } = {})`; `GET /todos?overdue=true`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test** — let `withServer(fn, store)` accept an optional store passed to `createApp(store)`. Test `filters overdue todos` with `createStore({ now: () => new Date('2026-10-23T23:30:00Z') })`: POST `past` (`2026-10-22`), `today` (`2026-10-23`), `future` (`2026-10-24`), `none` (no date), `donePast` (`2026-10-01`, then PATCH `done: true`).
+  - `GET /todos?overdue=true` titles → `['past']`.
+  - `GET /todos` → 5 todos; `GET /todos?overdue=false` → 5 todos.
+  - PATCH `donePast` `done: false` → filter titles `['past', 'donePast']`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run test, verify it fails** — `npm test`; expected: FAIL (filter returns all 5).
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** — store: today = `now().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`; overdue when `!todo.done && todo.dueDate !== null && todo.dueDate < today` (string compare). App: `store.list({ overdue: url.searchParams.get('overdue') === 'true' })`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests, verify they pass** — `npm test`; all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** — `git commit -am "feat: GET /todos?overdue=true (#1)"`
+
+### Task 3: List page — date, marker, filter checkbox
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `public/index.html`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `GET /todos`, `GET /todos?overdue=true` (Task 2).
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test** — extend `serves the list page`: body also matches `/data-testid="filter-overdue"/` and `/nur überfällige/`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run test, verify it fails** — `npm test`; FAIL on `filter-overdue`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** — above the list: `<label><input type="checkbox" data-testid="filter-overdue"> nur überfällige</label>`. Script: fetch both lists, build a `Set` of overdue ids, render function draws the full list or (checkbox checked) the overdue list; on `change` re-render (re-fetch both). Per item after `todo-title`: if `dueDate`, a `<span data-testid="todo-due">` with text `` ` · fällig ${d}.${m}.${y}` `` from splitting the string; if overdue, `<span data-testid="todo-overdue">` with text ` überfällig`. Use `textContent` only; no styles.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests, verify they pass** — `npm test`; all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** — `git commit -am "feat: show due dates and overdue filter on list page (#1)"`
